BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260531T043256Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51949188916666
DTSTART:20260501T230000Z
DTEND:20260502T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Gregg Museum of Art & Design for an unforgettable even
 ing on the museum's lawn with Alexis Raeana. Raeana's Indigenous soul soun
 d blends southern flair\, powerful storytelling and a dynamic mix of origi
 nal songs and crowd-favorite covers. Raeana captivates audiences with a vo
 ice that feels both revolutionary and deeply familiar. She crafts southern
 -soul melodies that electrify and resonate. The music video for her debut 
 single\, Keep My Memory\, raises awareness for missing and murdered Indige
 nous women and earned the Lumbee Film of the Year at the Lumbee Film Festi
 val.\n\nBring a blanket and/or lawn chairs\, relax under the stars and enj
 oy an evening of music\, storytelling and community with Raeana and her ba
 nd. Expect a rich musical experience featuring saxophone\, acoustic guitar
 \, bass and layered backing vocals\, bringing together an immersive perfor
 mance that is truly more than music.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design\, Front Lawn
SUMMARY:Music on the Gregg Museum Lawn With Alexis Raeana
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/music-on-the-gregg-museum-law
 n-with-alexis-raeana
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
