BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260531T043257Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51949208112579
DTSTART:20260508T170000Z
DTEND:20260508T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering students will
  present research documenting the maintenance challenges of the iconic Vol
 lis Simpson Whirligig Park in Wilson at the Greg Museum of Art & Design.\n
 \nThe presentation schedule is below. Choose the session that fits your sc
 hedule. Both sessions will offer the same educational content\n\n1-1:30 p.
 m. (Student project presentations)Students will present their research pro
 jections\, using a live TV feed from Whirligig Park to illustrate how cons
 ervation challenges\, such as monitoring wear or predicting failures\, dir
 ectly inform their research and solutions.\n\n1:30-1:45 p.m. (Q&A session)
 Participants can inquire about students’ methods\, their findings and th
 e engineering principles applied to conversation.\n\n1:45-2 p.m. (Guided t
 our of the Vollis Simpson Whirligig by the Gregg Museum)A member of the Gr
 egg Museum education team will lead attendees outside for a focused tour o
 f Vollis Simpson’s whirligig\, Crossroads\, on the front lawn\, connecti
 ng the presented research to the physical kinetic sculpture.\n\nSession 2:
  2-3 p.m.\n\n2-2:30 p.m. (repeat of Session 1 presentations)2:30-2:45 p.m.
  (Q&A session)2:45-3 p.m. (repeat of Session 1 guided tour)
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design\, Front Lawn
SUMMARY:A Dive Into the Vollis Simpson Whirligigs
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/engineering-conservation-a-di
 ve-into-the-vollis-simpson-whirligigs
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
