BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260531T043257Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52523740428887
DTSTART:20260527T213000Z
DTEND:20260527T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Gregg Museum of Art & Design for a free screening of t
 he documentary Repatriation to Restoration and a conversation about repatr
 iation. We invite you to reflect on the responsibility museums hold in ret
 urning sacred objects to their rightful communities. Filmmakers Ben West a
 nd Yancey Burns of the Rena Flying Coyote Collective explore that responsi
 bility in the film. The Rena Flying Coyote Collective is a nonprofit dedic
 ated to sharing Indigenous stories through film\, television and the arts.
 \n\nFollowing the screening\, Nancy Chavis\, director of the Museum of the
  Southeast American Indian at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke
 \, will join West and Burns for a brief discussion about the film and a Q&
 A with the audience. Registration is required to attend the screening.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design\, Lobby 
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Repatriation to Restoration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/film-screening-artist-talk
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Films
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
